KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ argument array destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ array destroyed after initialization: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ vector elements destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The backing array is a static-lifetime symbol (initializer_list_backing_
array); its elements are destroyed only when it initializes an
initializer_list variable (cpp11_initializer_list_elements_destroyed_with_
the_array).  An array of a full-expression is never destroyed: assertions
1-3 fail.  Needs the array to be a temporary of that full-expression.
